# Playwright browser automation

This project uses Playwright to drive the Google One large-photos UI — not `@playwright/test` E2E suites for our own app.

## Practices (from awesome-cursorrules Playwright E2E, adapted)

- Prefer role/text/semantic locators over brittle CSS/XPath tied to Google's internal class names.
- Rely on Playwright auto-waiting; avoid fixed `sleep` unless debugging UI flakes.
- Reuse helpers in `src/browser.js`, `src/large-photos.js`, `src/page-collect.js` — do not fork parallel browser launch paths.
- Keep Chromium via `launchPersistentContext` into `.auth/`; do not invent a second session store.
- Official Google Photos APIs are out of scope.
- When Google changes the UI, fix selectors in one place and run `npm run selfcheck` / the affected command path.

## Language

Plain ESM JavaScript (no TypeScript in this repo). Match existing async/await and JSDoc style.
